            "review_text": "A A\nMilan, Italy165 contributions\n0\nExcellent small central restaurant serving authentic vietnamese cuisine\nThe restaurant was right behind our hotel and based on the recommendation of a very good frind we decided to try it our first night in Saigon. To start we chose a great selection of appetizers including spring rolls and salads. As a main course we had fried soft shell clams and squid. Everything was really fresh and authentic. The bill was also surprisingly light for such a central location. Having had such a great experience we dedided to go again the following night and had ann equally excellent dinner.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 30, 2012",
